{"id":"hinu_ber","lemma":"hinüber","pos":"adv","rank":4276,"glosses":["across, over, there (towards a different side; in direction away from the speaker)","dead; spoiled, gone off; utterly broken, out of order"],"ipa":"/hɪˈnyːbəʁ/","audio":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/5/5a/De-hin%C3%BCber.ogg/De-hin%C3%BCber.ogg.mp3","examples":[{"text":"Die Blumen sind hinüber.","en":"The flowers are dead.","words":[{"g":"the"},{"g":"flower (small","l":"Blume"},{"g":"are","l":"sein"},null]},{"text":"Springen Sie hinüber.","en":"Jump across.","audio":"https://tatoeba.org/en/audio/download/389708","words":[{"g":"to spring"},{"g":"she / they / you"},null]},{"text":"Diese Orangen sind hinüber.","en":"These oranges have rotted.","words":[{"g":"this one, this","l":"dieser"},{"g":"orange","l":"Orange"},{"g":"are","l":"sein"},null]},{"text":"Ich bat Tom, hinüber zu gehen.","en":"I asked Tom to go there.","words":[{"g":"I"},{"g":"to ask","l":"bitten"},null,null,{"g":"to / too"},{"g":"to go, to walk"}]},{"text":"Tom ging zu Maria hinüber.","en":"Tom walked over to Mary.","words":[null,{"g":"to go, to walk","l":"gehen"},{"g":"to / too"},null,null]}]}